# 51. Mobile Validation Gate

A mobile design fails validation if:

- primary action is inaccessible;
- navigation disappears;
- critical information is unreadable;
- tables become unusable;
- dialogs overflow;
- text is clipped;
- touch targets are too small;
- essential functionality depends on hover.

---

# 52. Tablet Validation Gate

A tablet design fails if it simply compresses desktop content into unusable columns.

Tablet must have intentional composition.

---

# 53. Desktop Validation Gate

Desktop fails if:

- content is excessively sparse without purpose;
- information hierarchy is unclear;
- tables become decorative cards;
- shell consumes excessive space;
- dense workflows become visually noisy.

---

# 54. Accessibility Validation Gate

A page fails if:

- keyboard users cannot complete the primary workflow;
- focus is invisible;
- controls lack accessible names;
- form errors are not associated;
- status depends only on color;
- dialogs trap focus incorrectly;
- dynamic state is inaccessible.

