# 152. Blocking Issues

A blocking issue is any issue that could force widespread redesign.

Examples:

- uncertain typography;
- uncertain navigation;
- missing responsive strategy;
- missing AI state model;
- missing table strategy;
- missing accessibility model;
- contradictory tokens.

---

# 153. Non-Blocking Issues

Examples:

- minor spacing adjustment;
- small icon preference;
- copy refinement;
- image crop refinement.

Non-blocking issues may be handled during page design.

---

# 154. Foundation Change Control

After 06H is frozen, foundational changes require explicit change control.

A page-specific preference must not silently modify the global system.

